A shader editor that runs entirely in the browser over WebGPU. Write a
fragment shader, see it rendered live on a full-screen canvas, and share it
as a link — no account needed to try one out.

<ProjectGallery
	images={[
		{ src: "/projects/shaderkit/desktop.png", alt: "Shaderkit shader gallery desktop view", aspect: 1.6 },
		{ src: "/projects/shaderkit/mobile.png", alt: "Shaderkit shader gallery mobile view", aspect: 0.4621 },
	]}
/>

Every shader gets a small prelude bound automatically at group 0: elapsed
time, canvas resolution, and pointer position, all as one uniform struct.
A shader only has to declare `for_each_pixel` and it already has the inputs
most sandboxes make you wire up by hand:

```wgsl
struct Prelude {
  elapsed_sec: f32,
  resolution: vec2<u32>,
  pointer: vec2<u32>,
}

@binding(0) @group(0) var<uniform> prelude: Prelude;
```

```wgsl
@fragment
fn for_each_pixel(@builtin(position) pos: vec4f) -> @location(0) vec4f {
    var uv = pos.xy / vec2f(prelude.resolution);
    let color = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(prelude.elapsed_sec + uv.xyx + vec3(0.0, 2.0, 4.0));
    return vec4(color, 1.0);
}
```

![Shaderkit editor](/projects/shaderkit/editor.png)

Compiling untrusted WGSL from the browser means a broken shader can't be
allowed to take the renderer down with it. The editor wraps every build in
an error scope and reads the compilation log back out before swapping the
pipeline in, so a bad shader just reports why it failed instead of leaving a
blank canvas:

```ts
this.device.pushErrorScope("validation");
const shaderModule = this.device.createShaderModule({
	label: "user shader",
	code: wgslCode,
});
const compilationInfo = await shaderModule.getCompilationInfo();
if (compilationInfo.messages.some((m) => m.type === "error")) {
	throw compilationInfo;
}
```

The [editor]({editorLink}) is based on chromium's implementation of WebGPU, and expected to work best with it.
For other browsers and platforms, such as linux experimental flags or nightly versions might need to be enabled in order to work.
Here you can find an [up to date status](https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/wiki/Implementation-Status) for each browser and platform.

[Try it at shaderkit.dev]({config.platformLinks.shaderkit})
